  "id": "Compound::DB00554 - Gene::9356",
  "verbalization": "Piroxicam, a nonsteroidal anti-inflammatory drug, is shown to bind to Slc22a8, which is involved in the transport of organic anions, including those that are zwitterionic or cationic. This binding is further linked to Slc22a6, suggesting a potential role in the transport of such molecules across cellular membranes. The evidence is consistent across multiple paths, with Slc22a8 acting as a central mediator in the transport process, and Slc22a6 being a downstream participant in this pathway. The overlapping roles of Slc22a8 and Slc22a6 in transporting anionic and zwitterionic compounds imply a shared mechanism of action, possibly involving the regulation of ion transport across cell membranes. The integration of these pathways highlights the importance of Slc22a6 in the transport of charged molecules, and suggests that Piroxicam may influence this process through its interaction with Slc22a8.",
